6. CONDITIONS, TERMINATION, AND CURE

The permissions granted by this license remain effective only while
the licensee complies with its conditions.

If a licensee violates the applicable terms, the license to the
Software terminates automatically.

A licensee who becomes aware of a violation may restore compliance
by curing the violation within 30 days of:

  a. First becoming aware of the violation; or
  b. Receiving written notice identifying the violation;

whichever occurs first.

Curing a violation means taking reasonable and concrete steps to
resolve the specific non-compliance.

Examples include:

  - Restoring missing copyright or license notices.
  - Restoring removed Pixelian attribution.
  - Replacing "Powered by Pixelian.dev" with
    "Extends Pixelian.dev" after code modification.
  - Adding omitted "@modified-by" annotations.
  - Correcting an improperly renamed fork.
  - Removing misleading trademarks or branding.
  - Removing claims of official endorsement or authorship.

If an eligible violation is fully cured within the permitted period,
the license is automatically reinstated upon completion of the cure.

Reinstatement does not automatically waive liability for violations
that occurred before the cure.

A repeated violation of substantially the same obligation following
a previous cure, or a deliberate violation involving concealment,
misrepresentation, or bad faith, is not eligible for automatic
reinstatement.

In such cases, reinstatement requires express written permission
from the copyright holder.

A separate, unintentional violation of a different obligation may
qualify for its own cure period.

The copyright holder may grant additional reinstatement rights in
writing at their discretion.


