9. DEFINITIONS

"Software"

Means the original source code, stylesheets, data files, and
documentation distributed by Antranik Agopian under the Pixelian name
and made available at pixelian.dev, including protected portions
incorporated into modified versions.


"Application"

Means a website, web application, or other software product built
using the Software, whose primary purpose is to provide application
functionality rather than redistribute Pixelian as a reusable
framework, frontend template, boilerplate, or starter kit.


"Original Code File"

Means an executable source file originally distributed with the
Software, including JavaScript, CSS, PHP, and other source files
containing the Software's implementation.


"Code Modification"

Means changing, removing, replacing, or adapting original Pixelian
code, including modifications made to copied portions of that code.

Code Modifications include changes to original source files even
when the resulting behavior remains substantially the same.

Adding independently authored files without changing or adapting
original Pixelian code is not a Code Modification.


"Configuration Change"

Means editing configuration, metadata, or application-specific data
without changing original Pixelian executable code.

Configuration Changes include edits to data/*.json, robots.txt,
sitemap.xml, site.webmanifest, and placeholder substitutions
performed by setup.sh.

Configuration Changes do not trigger the modified attribution tier.


"Modify"

Means to change, remove, replace, or add to the contents of any file
originally distributed with the Software.

Not every modification is a Code Modification.

Configuration Changes and changes to non-code documentation may be
modifications in the general sense but are excluded from the
modified-code attribution tier.


"Fork"

Means a separately maintained or redistributed copy of the Software,
whether modified or unmodified, that is distributed as a reusable
framework, frontend template, boilerplate, or starter kit.

A fork remains subject to the name-preservation and attribution
requirements of this license.


"Substantial Portion"

Means original Pixelian code, styles, layouts, modules, or primitives
incorporated into another product in a manner that plays a material
functional or structural role.

An isolated, incidental code fragment does not automatically
constitute a substantial portion.


"Official Pixelian"

Means the version of the Software released or expressly designated
as official by the copyright holder or an authorized successor.

Independent forks are not official releases unless expressly
authorized in writing.


